WEBVTT

00:43:59.958 --> 00:44:01.226
AG: They're speechless.

00:44:01.250 --> 00:44:07.351
EP: But I think the foundation of that
is two different things

00:44:07.375 --> 00:44:09.226
and is actually quite serious.

00:44:09.250 --> 00:44:11.809
The first thing is
I fundamentally understand

00:44:11.833 --> 00:44:13.250
that I depend on others.

00:44:14.292 --> 00:44:18.393
I also fundamentally know
that my family's background

00:44:18.417 --> 00:44:19.934
shaped me very much about that.

00:44:19.958 --> 00:44:22.643
So I mean, the short nut of it is

00:44:22.667 --> 00:44:25.434
that my two parents
are the sole survivors of five years

00:44:25.458 --> 00:44:26.726
in concentration camps.

00:44:26.750 --> 00:44:28.601
They've lost their entire family.

00:44:28.625 --> 00:44:31.583
And boy, did they never think
that they survived on their own.